  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Task: Two integer arrays nums1 and nums2 are already sorted in non-decreasing order. The task is to output the median of the multiset formed by combining both arrays.\n\nFor an odd total number of elements, the median is the middle value. For an even total, it is the arithmetic mean of the two middle values. At least one array is non-empty.\n\nDesign a solution with O(log(min(m, n))) time complexity (binary search on the smaller array), where m and n are the input lengths.",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= m, n <= 1000",
      "1 <= m + n <= 2000",
      "-2147483648 <= nums1[i], nums2[i] <= 2147483647",
      "nums1 and nums2 are sorted in non-decreasing order"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of arguments: [nums1, nums2]. Example: [[1,3],[2]]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialized floating point number (median).",
    "notes": [
      "Preferred solution: binary search on the smaller array to partition both arrays so that left partitions contain the lower half of elements.",
      "Carefully handle empty arrays and even/odd combined lengths.",
      "Watch for integer overflow when computing sums of large integers; compute median using max/min and divide using double precision.",
      "Judge compares numeric results with standard double precision tolerance."
    ],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "[[1,3],[2]]",
        "output": "2.0",
        "explanation": "Combining and ordering the values gives [1, 2, 3]. With three values, the middle value 2 is the median."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "[[1,2],[3,4]]",
        "output": "2.5",
        "explanation": "The combined ordered sequence is [1, 2, 3, 4]. Its two middle values are 2 and 3, so the median is (2 + 3) / 2 = 2.5."
      }
    ]
  },
